DESCRIPTION Gotcha band: asks about a CRD/kind that almost certainly does not exist; the crew must verify the API surface.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "How many WorkloadProfile custom resources do we have, and which are in a Degraded phase?"
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 480 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

# Coordinator-answerable / correct stand-aside: do NOT assert specialist
# agreement (it would gate a correct answer to 0). Synthesis quality is
# judged by DEFER REFLECTS below.
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)

# Deterministic, drift-tolerant ground truth: no WorkloadProfile CRD exists; the answer should name it to deny existence. "Degraded" is not forbidden: a correct denial ("none in a Degraded phase") contains it; a fabricated phase count is the judge's to catch.
ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "WorkloadProfile")

# Reference-grounded quality: the deferred LLM judge (kubemoot-fitness crew) scores
# the synthesis against this ground truth on method and honesty, not specific values.
ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "No CRD of kind WorkloadProfile is registered on this cluster, so there are zero such custom resources and no phases to report. A correct answer verifies the registered API surface and states plainly that the kind is not installed, rather than inventing instances or a Degraded count. (the exact CRD set may drift; the constant is checking whether the named kind is actually registered before counting.)")
